<title>PAKISTAN: HOCKEY-FORMER PAKISTAN CAPTAIN DIES.</title>
<headline>HOCKEY-FORMER PAKISTAN CAPTAIN DIES.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former Pakistan hockey captain Qazi Mohib died on Sunday after a long illness, according to reports from the official Associated Press of Pakistan (APP). He was 37.</p>
<p>Mohib, who leaves a widow and young daughter, developed cancer on his right thigh and was admitted to a hospital in Peshawar 10 days ago, the APP said.</p>
<p>He played more than 150 internationals for Pakistan and captained the side for three years, taking them to major tournaments such as the Olympics, the Champions trophy and the World Cup.</p>
</text>
